10. FINANCIAL MODELING REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Use the actual canonical financial logic rather than an oversimplified ROI calculator.

Modeled annualized EBITDA:

EBITDA uplift =
incremental recovered service contribution
+ separately attributable scheduling contribution
+ avoided operating costs
- incremental running costs

Service contribution must be calculated using the current fill-rate improvement, contribution per fill-rate point, and recovery calibration defined in the reference engine.

Separate:
- EBITDA benefit
- Network working-capital release
- ACPL-owned working-capital cash realization

Network working-capital release is for operational and gate certification.

ONLY realized ACPL-owned working-capital release enters the applicable free cash-flow model.

Never add working-capital release to recurring EBITDA.

Use the original 60-month cash-flow model for:
- Timing of benefits
- Conditional funding tranches
- Cash-conversion assumptions
- Owned working-capital releases
- NPV at 18%
- Annualized IRR
- Durable payback month

For IRR:
Use time-phased cash flows and a numerical solver.
Do not derive IRR by dividing annual profit by investment.

Display uncomputable or undefined IRRs as N/A.

The current model assumes that operating EBITDA converts into incremental pre-tax cash at an assumed rate. Clearly disclose this.

The avoided-cost share must satisfy the relevant 40% financial guardrail according to the reference model.

